# The variables of Docker Compose. Copy this file, then write the values:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Docker Compose reads `.env` near `compose.yaml`, and it writes these two
# values in that file. Keep no value in this file: `.gitignore` keeps `.env`
# out of git, but it keeps this file under version control.
#
# `compose.yaml` holds DATABASE_URL and PORT with a value. Those two variables
# are not here, because Docker Compose reads no value of this file for them.
#
# Node reads no `.env` file. For development, `npm run dev:server` gives a key
# and the origin of the client of Vite. Paragraph 4.3 of `docs/architecture.md`
# gives each variable of the server.

# Better Auth signs the cookies and the tokens with this key. The server writes
# a message and it stops without this value. A new key removes each session, thus
# each user must sign in again. Make a key with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=

# The origin of the application, with the name of the reverse proxy, for example
# https://yume.example.com. Better Auth refuses a request from an other origin.
# With no value, the server uses http://localhost:3000.
#
# A browser removes a session cookie on a plain HTTP connection, because Yume
# sends that cookie with the attribute `secure`. Therefore this origin needs
# TLS. Paragraph 7 of `docs/architecture.md` gives the three tools, and
# paragraph 4.3 gives the rule of that attribute.
BETTER_AUTH_URL=
